<title>JAPAN: Nikko Sec, Daiwa Sec slump on racketeer report.</title>
<headline>Nikko Sec, Daiwa Sec slump on racketeer report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Nikko Securities Co Ltd and Daiwa Securities Co Ltd shares slumped on Monday afternoon, following a news report that a corporate racketeer had told prosecutors the brokerages conducted illegal stock deals for him, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0444 GMT, Nikko shares were down 54 yen or 7.16 percent at 700 yen, the largest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo bourse. It was also the sixth most heavily traded issue with trade totalling 3.07 million shares.</p>
<p>Daiwa shed 43 yen to 906 on turnover of 3.13 million shares, making it the seventh most heavily traded issue.</p>
</text>
